Changes:

1. src/types.ts — added "market" to the BuildingKind union.

2. src/buildings/registry.ts
   - BUILDING_REGISTRY: market: { cost: { wood: 20, stone: 15 }, requires: "storehouse" }. Because availability.ts and actions.ts read entirely from this table, build/availableBuildings/lockedBuildings etc. now enforce the storehouse prerequisite automatically.
   - BuildingCategory: added a "trade" category and mapped market to it (the Record<BuildingKind, BuildingCategory> type forces an entry; market isn't shelter/production/storage/defense, so a new category is the honest fit).
   - Updated the prerequisite-chain doc comment to include storehouse -> market.

3. src/sim/trade.ts (new)
   - export const SOLD_PER_STONE = 2 — the 2:1 ratio, "sold per stone".
   - export function sellResource(settlement, resource, amount): Settlement — throws "cannot sell: no market built" if no market stands; otherwise sells min(amount, held) (clamped at 0), converts at floor(sold / 2) stone, never drops the sold resource below 0, and returns a new settlement (no mutation). It reuses the resources/costs.ts credit() helper — which its doc comment already anticipated for exactly this feature.

4. src/sim/index.ts — exports sellResource and SOLD_PER_STONE alongside the other sim exports.

Verified behavior: 51 wood sold -> 0 wood, +25 stone (odd unit unconverted); selling more than held sells only the stock (5 wood -> 2 stone); zero stock is a no-op; works for food and stone too; throws without a market; input settlement untouched.

